## DBsubject('Calculus - multivariable')
## DBchapter('Differentiation of multivariable functions')
## DBsection('Chain rule')

DOCUMENT();

loadMacros("PGstandard.pl", "PGML.pl", "MathObjects.pl");

TEXT(beginproblem());

BEGIN_PGML
An ant is moving along a helical path [` \gamma(t) = (3\cos t,3\sin t,5t) `]. The temperature in space is given by [` f(x,y,z) = xy + z^2 `] in Celsius.

What is the velocity of the ant at [` t = 2\pi `]?

[` \gamma'(t) = `] ([________]{Real(0)}, [________]{Real(3)}, [________]{Real(5)}).

At what rate does the ant detect the temperature to be changing at [` t = \frac{3\pi}{4} `]?

[` \frac{\partial}{\partial t}f(\frac{3\pi}{4}) = `][________]{Compute("75pi/2")}
END_PGML

$showPartialCorrectAnswers = 0;

ENDDOCUMENT();